            <title>[LU-20414] Upstream workflow</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20414</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;At some point it will be useful to have a tool which can somewhat intelligently apply kernel mail list patches to lustre and lustre patches to the kernel for submission.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;$ contrib/scripts/lustre-kernel-sync.py --lustre ~/w/lustre-release --linux ~/w/linux --mode linux-to-lustre -v -h
usage: lustre-kernel-sync.py [-h] [-r LUSTRE] [-l LINUX] [-m MODE] [-g] [-v] [-n]

Copy files between linux and lustre

options:
  -h, --help           show this help message and exit
  -r, --lustre LUSTRE  Output file name (default: /home/shaun/w/lreview/contrib/lustre-release)
  -l, --linux LINUX    Kernel kernel headers (default: /home/shaun/w/lreview/contrib/scripts)
  -m, --mode MODE      mode default: 'linux-to-lustre'
  -g, --debug          Enable extra debug messages, default: No
  -v, --verbose        Enable extra messages, default: No
  -n, --dryrun         Dry run make to changes to any files default: No
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
